              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hydrangea is a plant that grows in cooler climates in the Himalayan region and the North-eastern states. It gives flowers of different colours, depending on the nature of the soil. Acidic soil produces bluecoloured flowers, whereas in basic soil, the flowers are"
