          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "pink or red. Can gardeners alter the colour of hydrangea flowers bypink or red. Can gardeners alter the colour of hydrangea flowers by adjusting the acidic or basic nature of the soil?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.44,
            0.647,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.1.3 Turmeric as an indicator"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.468,
            0.883,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have used blue and red litmus paper strips in Activity 2.1. Can you also make paper strips with some other natural indicators? Find out by performing the following activity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.539,
            0.544,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 2.5: Let us prepare"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.57,
            0.883,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take a spoonful of turmeric (haldi) in a petri dish or container and add a little water to make a paste (Fig. 2.9a). You may also grind a piece of fresh turmeric."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.631,
            0.882,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Carefully dip a piece of filter paper in the turmeric paste until it gets yellow colour."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.673,
            0.591,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take it out and allow it to dry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.697,
            0.882,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cut this yellow paper into thin strips, which are used as ‘turmeric paper’ (Fig. 2.9b)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.218,
            0.737,
            0.819,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Caution",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " — Perform this step under the supervision of an adult."
            }
          ]
        },
